@startuml
title D-03 Site Group and Site Reporting View Diagram
left to right direction

rectangle "Site Group\nLookup / Payment Scope" as SG {
  rectangle "WebPay/APM entry scope"
  rectangle "Customer search scope"
  rectangle "Channel experience metrics"
}

rectangle "Site\nReporting / Contract /\nVendor / POS / Operations Boundary" as SiteA {
  rectangle "Revenue attribution"
  rectangle "Vendor PMS mapping"
  rectangle "Site POS Server"
  rectangle "Operational exceptions"
}

rectangle "Site\nReporting / Contract /\nVendor / POS / Operations Boundary" as SiteB {
  rectangle "Revenue attribution"
  rectangle "Vendor PMS mapping"
  rectangle "Site POS Server"
  rectangle "Operational exceptions"
}

rectangle "Dashboard Views" as Dash {
  rectangle "Site Group view:\ncustomer channel scope"
  rectangle "Site view:\nfinancial/fiscal/operations attribution"
  rectangle "Portfolio view:\nauthorized aggregation"
}

SG --> SiteA : may resolve to
SG --> SiteB : special case may include
SiteA --> Dash
SiteB --> Dash
SG --> Dash

note bottom
Default case: one Site Group has one Site.
Special case: one Site Group may contain multiple Sites.
Financial and fiscal reporting uses resolved Site as primary attribution boundary.
end note
@enduml
